  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dan dan noodles are built on the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ma-la"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ma la"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " balance. The sauce should be simultaneously sesame-rich, chilli-hot, and garlicky. The pork topping adds texture and savouriness. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ya-cai"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Ya cai"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is worth seeking out from a Chinese supermarket. Without it the pork topping lacks its characteristic texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sesame-paste-chinese"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sesame paste"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " goes into the sauce cold. Thin it with the hot noodle cooking water just before serving. This emulsifies the sauce and brings everything together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
